From: Rémi Bernon <rbernon@codeweavers.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Flush GL commands when activating another context.

Backport of WineHQ commit 1c144117a8 (wine-11.17), adapted. Upstream adds
the flush at the start of macdrv_context_activate(), a function a later
upstream refactor split out of the base's macdrv_make_current(). The same
line is placed at the matching point here: after the release path and
before the new context is selected, while NtCurrentTeb()->glReserved2
still holds the context being left. Commands queued on that context reach
the GPU before another one becomes current.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
index 2fd17ac..b476f80 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
@@ -2311,6 +2311,8 @@ static BOOL macdrv_make_current(struct opengl_drawable *draw_base, struct opengl
         return TRUE;
     }
 
+    if (NtCurrentTeb()->glReserved2) funcs->p_glFlush();
+
     context->read_hwnd = context->draw_hwnd = NULL;
     context->read_view = context->draw_view = NULL;
     context->read_pbuffer = context->draw_pbuffer = NULL;
